    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Full suite is green (53 tests, 0 failures/errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the membership-level-4 tenure rule in `OwnerMapper.membershipLevel(Owner)` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`).\n\nThe level calculation still starts at 1 and adds 1 for having an email and 1 for having no namesakes. I added a **fourth factor**: +1 when the owner's tenure \u2014 `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now())` \u2014 is **more than 365 days**, and raised the cap from 3 to 4.\n\nBecause a newly created owner's `registrationDate` is today, its tenure is 0, so the tenure factor never applies at creation. A new owner with an email and `namesakeCount == 0` therefore tops out at `1 + 1 + 1 = 3`, never 4 \u2014 exactly as the spec and the new `Cp39Tests` require. Only owners whose tenure exceeds 365 days can reach level 4.\n\nAll 53 tests pass, including the membership tests `Cp39`, `Cp24`, `Cp23`, and `Cp15`.",
